   "source": [
    "def extract_amount(series):\n",
    "    numeric_str = series.str.replace(r\"^\\D+\", \"\", regex=True).str.replace(\",\", \"\", regex=False)\n",
    "    return pd.to_numeric(numeric_str, errors=\"coerce\")\n",
    "\n",
    "df[\"total_spent_value\"] = extract_amount(df[\"total_spent\"])\n",
    "df[\"cost_per_gallon_value\"] = extract_amount(df[\"cost_per_gallon\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "df[[\"total_spent\", \"total_spent_value\", \"cost_per_gallon\", \"cost_per_gallon_value\"]].sample(10, random_state=1)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "aad284c4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q2.3: Car make, model, year, User ID\n",
    "\n",
    "Extracted `car_make`, `car_model`, `car_year`, and `user_id` from `user_url` using the expected\n",
    "`/make/model/year/id` URL structure. [0.33]% of URLs did not match this pattern — inspecting these\n",
    "showed malformed entries (e.g. a missing slash between make and model, such as\n",
    "\".../kianival/2009/789684\" instead of \".../kia/nival/2009/789684\"). These are left as NaN rather\n",
    "than guessed at, since splitting a merged make+model string reliably would require an external\n",
    "lookup of known car makes, which is out of scope here."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "id": "ea2b5c35",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "0.33% of user_url values didn't match the expected /make/model/year/id pattern\n"
     ]
