   ],
   "source": [
    "#2.3\n",
    "extracted = df[\"user_url\"].str.extract(r\"/([^/]+)/([^/]+)/(\\d{4})/(\\d+)/?$\")\n",
    "extracted.columns = [\"car_make\", \"car_model\", \"car_year\", \"user_id\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "df[\"car_make\"] = extracted[\"car_make\"]\n",
    "df[\"car_model\"] = extracted[\"car_model\"]\n",
    "df[\"car_year\"] = pd.to_numeric(extracted[\"car_year\"])\n",
    "df[\"user_id\"] = extracted[\"user_id\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "pct_unmatched = df[\"car_make\"].isna().mean() * 100\n",
    "print(f\"{pct_unmatched:.2f}% of user_url values didn't match the expected /make/model/year/id pattern\")\n",
    "\n",
    "df[[\"user_url\", \"car_make\", \"car_model\", \"car_year\", \"user_id\"]].sample(5, random_state=1)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3eb77480",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q2.4–2.6: Unit conversions (litres, km, litres/100km)\n",
    "\n",
    "Converted gallons to litres and miles to km using **US gallon** conventions\n",
    "(1 US gal = 3.785411784 L, 1 mile = 1.609344 km) rather than UK/imperial gallons.\n",
    "This choice is based on: (1) the dominant currencies in this dataset ($, CA$, AU$, NZ$)\n",
    "point to US/North America/Oceania users rather than UK ones, and (2) the observed mpg\n",
    "distribution (mean ~22, median ~22) matches typical US-gallon fuel economy figures —\n",
    "imperial-gallon mpg for the same real efficiency would read roughly 20% higher.\n",
    "\n",
    "Computed litres_per_100km = (litres_filled / km_driven) * 100. Note: rows with\n",
    "km_driven == 0 produce inf/NaN here; these are left as-is for now and will be\n",
    "addressed during outlier removal in Section 4."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 22,
   "id": "22bba1ac",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
