    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "users_per_currency = df.groupby(\"currency\")[\"user_url\"].nunique().sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "print(users_per_currency.head(20))\n",
    "\n",
    "top_n = 20\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
    "users_per_currency.head(top_n).plot(kind=\"bar\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"currency (proxy for country)\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"number of unique users\")\n",
    "plt.title(f\"Unique users per currency (top {top_n})\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "165481f0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q3.2: Unique users per day (app popularity)\n",
    "\n",
    "Plotted daily unique-user counts (`user_url`) with a 30-day rolling average overlay to reduce\n",
    "day-to-day noise. The shape mirrors the fueling-date distribution from Q1.1.5 (growth through\n",
    "2019, a dip around 2020, a sharp ramp into 2022, then an abrupt cliff to zero) — consistent with\n",
    "the earlier conclusion that this reflects a hard data-collection cutoff around mid-2022, not a\n",
    "genuine collapse in app usage."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 24,
   "id": "fd56175b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1400x500 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "users_per_day = df.groupby(df[\"date_fueled\"].dt.floor(\"D\"))[\"user_url\"].nunique()\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "users_per_day.plot(alpha=0.4, label=\"daily\")\n",
    "users_per_day.rolling(30).mean().plot(label=\"30-day rolling average\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"date\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"unique users\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Unique users per day (app popularity over time)\")\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ef38dfdd",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q3.3: Distribution of vehicle age per country\n",
    "\n",
    "Computed vehicle age as (year of date_fueled - car_year), relative to the fill-up date rather\n",
    "than today's date, per the brief's instruction. Compared the top 8 currencies via boxplot, with\n",
    "age clipped to [0, 40] years purely for plot readability (a few bad car_year extractions from\n",
    "Step 11's URL parsing would otherwise dominate the axis; this is not real outlier removal, which\n",
    "is scoped to Section 4)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 25,
   "id": "4c0b4c39",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1200x600 with 0 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "top_currencies = df[\"currency\"].value_counts().head(8).index\n",
    "subset = df[df[\"currency\"].isin(top_currencies)].copy()\n",
    "subset[\"vehicle_age\"] = subset[\"date_fueled\"].dt.year - subset[\"car_year\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "# clip to a sane age range purely for plotting, so a few bad car_year extractions don't wreck the axis\n",
    "subset = subset[subset[\"vehicle_age\"].between(0, 40)]\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
    "subset.boxplot(column=\"vehicle_age\", by=\"currency\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"currency (country proxy)\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"vehicle age (years) at time of fill-up\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Distribution of vehicle age per country\")\n",
    "plt.suptitle(\"\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "81fd3d25",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q3.4: Most popular vehicle makes and models\n",
    "\n",
    "Deduplicated to one row per user (via `user_url`) before counting, so popularity reflects\n",
    "number of distinct owners rather than number of logged fill-up transactions — otherwise a\n",
    "handful of very active loggers would distort the ranking. Plotted the top 15 makes and top 15\n",
    "specific make/model combinations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 26,
   "id": "72ed26d8",
   "metadata": {},
