  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cf30fb14",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q4.1.2: Outlier removal per currency\n",
    "\n",
    "Used Tukey's IQR method (flagging values outside [Q1 - 1.5*IQR, Q3 + 1.5*IQR]) applied\n",
    "*separately per currency* on total_spent_value, litres_filled, cost_per_litre, and\n",
    "litres_per_100km. This adapts automatically to each currency's own scale rather than needing\n",
    "hand-picked thresholds per currency. cost_per_litre specifically targets the brief's own example\n",
    "of SA users mislabeled with `$` currency (their implied price-per-litre in USD terms would be\n",
    "absurdly high). Rows with missing/infinite values in these fields were dropped separately first,\n",
    "since IQR bounds can't be computed sensibly around undefined values."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 28,
   "id": "4a363f6c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Dropping 118908 rows with missing/infinite values in checked fields\n",
      "   $ | total_spent_value : bounds=(   -7.02,    93.81), flagged=46477\n",
      "   $ | litres_filled     : bounds=(    5.50,    90.17), flagged=20404\n",
      "   $ | cost_per_litre    : bounds=(    0.26,     1.52), flagged=53003\n",
      "   $ | litres_per_100km  : bounds=(    1.22,    21.02), flagged=28124\n",
      "   £ | total_spent_value : bounds=(   -2.85,   111.44), flagged=1239\n",
      "   £ | litres_filled     : bounds=(    1.73,    85.20), flagged=918\n",
      "   £ | cost_per_litre    : bounds=(    0.86,     1.66), flagged=4455\n",
      "   £ | litres_per_100km  : bounds=(    1.04,    14.73), flagged=3602\n",
      "   € | total_spent_value : bounds=(    0.52,   116.01), flagged=1497\n",
      "   € | litres_filled     : bounds=(    3.57,    82.05), flagged=581\n",
      "   € | cost_per_litre    : bounds=(    0.73,     2.02), flagged=2723\n",
      "   € | litres_per_100km  : bounds=(    1.62,    13.34), flagged=2910\n",
      " CA$ | total_spent_value : bounds=(   -1.25,   117.55), flagged=1050\n",
      " CA$ | litres_filled     : bounds=(    5.81,    84.31), flagged=1188\n",
      " CA$ | cost_per_litre    : bounds=(    0.66,     1.94), flagged=1364\n",
      " CA$ | litres_per_100km  : bounds=(    1.52,    20.03), flagged=1597\n",
      "   R | total_spent_value : bounds=( -106.64,  1565.05), flagged=1109\n",
      "   R | litres_filled     : bounds=(   -0.95,   101.27), flagged=1171\n",
      "   R | cost_per_litre    : bounds=(    7.18,    22.03), flagged=793\n",
      "   R | litres_per_100km  : bounds=(    1.59,    18.05), flagged=1351\n",
      "\n",
      "Starting rows (top 5 currencies): 971644\n",
      "After dropping missing/infinite:   852736\n",
      "Flagged as outliers (IQR):         114299 (13.40% of 852736)\n",
      "Final clean rows:                  738437 (76.00% of original top-5 rows retained)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "df[\"cost_per_litre\"] = df[\"cost_per_gallon_value\"] / US_GALLON_TO_LITRES\n",
    "\n",
    "check_cols = [\"total_spent_value\", \"litres_filled\", \"cost_per_litre\", \"litres_per_100km\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "df_top5 = df[df[\"currency\"].isin(top5_list)].copy()\n",
    "n_before = len(df_top5)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Step A: can't judge rows with missing/infinite values in the fields we're checking -- drop them\n",
    "df_top5[check_cols] = df_top5[check_cols].replace([np.inf, -np.inf], np.nan)\n",
    "valid_mask = df_top5[check_cols].notna().all(axis=1)\n",
    "print(f\"Dropping {(~valid_mask).sum()} rows with missing/infinite values in checked fields\")\n",
    "df_top5 = df_top5.loc[valid_mask].copy()\n",
    "n_after_missing_drop = len(df_top5)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Step B: per-currency Tukey IQR fences on each field\n",
    "def iqr_bounds(series, k=1.5):\n",
    "    q1, q3 = series.quantile([0.25, 0.75])\n",
    "    iqr = q3 - q1\n",
    "    return q1 - k * iqr, q3 + k * iqr\n",
    "\n",
    "is_outlier = pd.Series(False, index=df_top5.index)\n",
    "for cur in top5_list:\n",
    "    mask_cur = df_top5[\"currency\"] == cur\n",
    "    for col in check_cols:\n",
    "        lo, hi = iqr_bounds(df_top5.loc[mask_cur, col])\n",
    "        flagged = mask_cur & ((df_top5[col] < lo) | (df_top5[col] > hi))\n",
    "        is_outlier |= flagged\n",
    "        print(f\"{cur:>4} | {col:<18}: bounds=({lo:8.2f}, {hi:8.2f}), flagged={flagged.sum()}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "df_clean = df_top5.loc[~is_outlier].copy()\n",
    "n_final = len(df_clean)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nStarting rows (top 5 currencies): {n_before}\")\n",
    "print(f\"After dropping missing/infinite:   {n_after_missing_drop}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Flagged as outliers (IQR):         {is_outlier.sum()} ({is_outlier.mean()*100:.2f}% of {n_after_missing_drop})\")\n",
    "print(f\"Final clean rows:                  {n_final} ({n_final/n_before*100:.2f}% of original top-5 rows retained)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "d6d1844b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q4.1.2 & Q4.1.3: Outlier removal per currency, and how many were removed\n",
    "\n",
    "Of 971,644 transactions across the top 5 currencies, 118,908 (12.2%) were dropped for having\n",
    "missing/infinite values in the checked fields (total_spent_value, litres_filled, cost_per_litre,\n",
    "litres_per_100km) — higher than the ~6.3% baseline missingness of any single field, since this\n",
    "is the union across four independently-missing columns.\n",
    "\n",
    "Of the remaining 852,736 rows, Tukey's IQR method (per currency, k=1.5) flagged 114,299 (13.4%)\n",
    "as outliers in at least one field. `$` had by far the most flags, notably on cost_per_litre\n",
    "(53,003) — plausibly because `$`, being the most generic/default currency symbol, absorbs\n",
    "misconfigured users from many countries, not just the SA example given in the brief. As a sanity\n",
    "check, Rand's cost_per_litre bounds (R7.18-R22.03) line up well with real-world SA fuel prices\n",
    "over this period, supporting that the method is producing sensible thresholds rather than\n",
    "arbitrary ones.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Total removed: 233,207 of 971,644 rows (24.00%). Final clean dataset: 738,437 rows.**"
   ]
  },
