     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "## Corrected RF\n",
    "model_features_clean = [\"km_driven\", \"vehicle_age\", \"odometer\", \"car_make\", \"car_model\", \"currency\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "model_df2 = df_clean[model_features_clean + [\"litres_per_100km\"]].dropna().copy()\n",
    "for col in [\"car_make\", \"car_model\", \"currency\"]:\n",
    "    model_df2[col] = model_df2[col].astype(\"category\").cat.codes\n",
    "\n",
    "X2 = model_df2[model_features_clean]\n",
    "y2 = model_df2[\"litres_per_100km\"]\n",
    "X2_train, X2_test, y2_train, y2_test = train_test_split(X2, y2, test_size=0.2, random_state=42)\n",
    "\n",
    "rf2 = RandomForestRegressor(n_estimators=100, max_depth=12, random_state=42, n_jobs=-1)\n",
    "rf2.fit(X2_train, y2_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "importances2 = pd.Series(rf2.feature_importances_, index=model_features_clean).sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
    "print(importances2)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(8, 5))\n",
    "importances2.plot(kind=\"barh\")\n",
    "plt.gca().invert_yaxis()\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"importance\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Random Forest feature importance (leakage-free) for litres_per_100km\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"\\nTrain R²: {rf2.score(X2_train, y2_train):.3f}   Test R²: {rf2.score(X2_test, y2_test):.3f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2628eea5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q4.2.9: Random Forest feature importance (corrected model)\n",
    "\n",
    "| feature | importance |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| km_driven   | 0.489 |\n",
    "| car_model   | 0.289 |\n",
    "| car_make    | 0.095 |\n",
    "| currency    | 0.082 |\n",
    "| vehicle_age | 0.035 |\n",
    "| odometer    | 0.010 |\n",
    "\n",
    "Train R²=0.675, Test R²=0.668 — close together (no overfitting), and far more believable than\n",
    "the leaky model's 0.99. km_driven remains the dominant feature (consistent with its -0.53\n",
    "correlation from Q4.2.8), confirming the brief's expectation, with the same mechanical caveat as\n",
    "before. car_model emerges as the second most important feature (0.289) — something correlation\n",
    "alone structurally could not test — directly confirming the brief's prediction that model matters.\n",
    "car_make and currency also show meaningful importance, with currency in particular revealing a\n",
    "country-level effect the correlation matrix couldn't capture at all. vehicle_age and odometer\n",
    "rank lower here (0.035, 0.010) than their raw correlations (0.21, 0.15) might suggest; since the\n",
    "two are themselves correlated (0.61), the Random Forest likely spreads credit for their shared\n",
    "information unevenly rather than either being unimportant on its own. The remaining ~33% of\n",
    "unexplained variance is consistent with confounding factors this dataset doesn't capture (engine\n",
    "size, fuel type, aircon use, load, weather, transmission), as the brief itself anticipates."
   ]
  },
