    "\n",
    "The monthly average cost_per_litre for SA closely tracks real, documented South African fuel\n",
    "price history: a dip around 2008-09 (global financial crisis), a rise through 2009-2014, a sharp\n",
    "drop 2014-2016 (matching the global oil price collapse), a rise to a 2018/19 peak, a sharp dip\n",
    "around 2020 (COVID-19 oil price crash), and a steep climb through 2021-2022 to record highs\n",
    "(post-COVID recovery and 2022 energy crisis). Reproducing these known real-world events gives\n",
    "strong confidence that the currency extraction and cost conversion pipeline (Sections 2 and 4.1)\n",
    "is producing accurate, trustworthy values."
   ]
