   ],
   "source": [
    "sa_df[\"day_of_week\"] = sa_df[\"date_fueled\"].dt.day_name()\n",
    "\n",
    "day_order = [\"Monday\", \"Tuesday\", \"Wednesday\", \"Thursday\", \"Friday\", \"Saturday\", \"Sunday\"]\n",
    "counts_by_day = sa_df[\"day_of_week\"].value_counts().reindex(day_order)\n",
    "print(counts_by_day)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\n",
    "colors = [\"tab:orange\" if day == \"Tuesday\" else \"tab:blue\" for day in day_order]\n",
    "counts_by_day.plot(kind=\"bar\", color=colors)\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"day of week\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"number of fill-ups\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"SA fill-ups by day of week (Tuesday highlighted)\")\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=45)\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e2537558",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q4.3.4: Reduced to first Tuesday / first Wednesday only (comment)\n",
    "\n",
    "Of 2,240 matching entries, 1,419 (63%) fall on the first Tuesday vs. 821 (37%) on the first\n",
    "Wednesday — a substantial imbalance even before accounting for price direction. This suggests a\n",
    "general tendency to refuel on the actual price-change day rather than routinely waiting; whether\n",
    "this pattern is driven specifically by rising prices (Q4.3.7) or holds regardless of direction\n",
    "will need the price-direction breakdown next."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 41,
   "id": "bbc3f51e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "(2240, 23)\n",
      "day_of_week\n",
      "Tuesday      1419\n",
      "Wednesday     821\n",
      "Name: count, dtype: int64\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "sa_df[\"day_of_month\"] = sa_df[\"date_fueled\"].dt.day\n",
    "\n",
    "is_first_tuesday = (sa_df[\"day_of_week\"] == \"Tuesday\") & (sa_df[\"day_of_month\"] <= 7)\n",
    "is_first_wednesday = (sa_df[\"day_of_week\"] == \"Wednesday\") & (sa_df[\"day_of_month\"] <= 7)\n",
    "\n",
    "tues_wed_df = sa_df[is_first_tuesday | is_first_wednesday].copy()\n",
    "print(tues_wed_df.shape)\n",
    "print(tues_wed_df[\"day_of_week\"].value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "667b8cfb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q4.3.5: Price direction indicator\n",
    "\n",
    "Derived a monthly price-direction label (\"up\"/\"down\") from month-over-month change in average\n",
    "cost_per_litre (validated against real SA fuel price history in Q4.3.2), then mapped it onto\n",
    "each first-Tuesday/first-Wednesday row. "
   ]
