   "source": [
    "monthly_price = sa_df.groupby(sa_df[\"date_fueled\"].dt.to_period(\"M\"))[\"cost_per_litre\"].mean()\n",
    "price_direction = monthly_price.diff().apply(lambda x: \"up\" if x > 0 else (\"down\" if x < 0 else \"no_change\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "tues_wed_df[\"month\"] = tues_wed_df[\"date_fueled\"].dt.to_period(\"M\")\n",
    "tues_wed_df[\"price_direction\"] = tues_wed_df[\"month\"].map(price_direction)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(tues_wed_df[\"price_direction\"].value_counts())\n",
    "tues_wed_df[[\"date_fueled\", \"day_of_week\", \"month\", \"price_direction\"]].sample(10, random_state=1)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "273e167c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Q4.3.6 & Q4.3.7: Refuelling behaviour by price direction (results)\n",
    "\n",
    "| price direction | Tuesday % | Wednesday % |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| down (n=648)  | 42.6% | 57.4% |\n",
    "| up (n=1592)   | 71.8% | 28.2% |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Q4.3.6 — Yes.** When prices are set to drop, 57.4% of first-Tuesday/Wednesday fill-ups happen\n",
    "on the Wednesday (vs. only 28.2% in up-months) — clear evidence that drivers postpone refuelling\n",
    "by a day to catch the lower price when they know it's coming.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Q4.3.7 — Yes, and more strongly.** When prices are set to rise, 71.8% of these fill-ups happen\n",
    "on the Tuesday itself (vs. only 42.6% in down-months) — drivers rush to fill up before the price\n",
    "increase takes effect. This effect is larger than the postponement effect in Q4.3.6 (a ~2.5:1\n",
    "Tuesday:Wednesday split vs. a ~1.35:1 Wednesday:Tuesday split), suggesting the \"avoid a price\n",
    "increase\" motivation is stronger than the \"wait for a price decrease\" motivation — consistent\n",
    "with loss aversion (people react more strongly to avoiding a cost than securing an equivalent\n",
    "saving)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 43,
   "id": "85832da7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "day_of_week      Tuesday  Wednesday  total  pct_tuesday  pct_wednesday\n",
      "price_direction                                                       \n",
      "down                 276        372    648    42.592593      57.407407\n",
      "up                  1143        449   1592    71.796482      28.203518\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x500 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "comparison = (\n",
    "    tues_wed_df.dropna(subset=[\"price_direction\"])\n",
    "    .groupby([\"price_direction\", \"day_of_week\"])\n",
    "    .size()\n",
    "    .unstack(\"day_of_week\")\n",
    ")\n",
    "comparison[\"total\"] = comparison[[\"Tuesday\", \"Wednesday\"]].sum(axis=1)\n",
    "comparison[\"pct_tuesday\"] = comparison[\"Tuesday\"] / comparison[\"total\"] * 100\n",
    "comparison[\"pct_wednesday\"] = comparison[\"Wednesday\"] / comparison[\"total\"] * 100\n",
    "print(comparison)\n",
    "\n",
    "comparison[[\"pct_tuesday\", \"pct_wednesday\"]].plot(kind=\"bar\", figsize=(8, 5))\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"% of first-Tuesday/first-Wednesday fill-ups\")\n",
    "plt.title(\"Refuelling day split by price direction that month\")\n",
    "plt.xticks(rotation=0)\n",
    "plt.legend(title=\"day\")\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  }
 ],
